 {
  "source": "Bernstein",
  "title": "Global Electrical Infrastructure: Pulse check on the data center build out, power gen lead times and international competition",
  "type": "sector",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-07-22",
  "insights": [
   "Data center construction is facing increased delays and cancellations in 2026, driven by public opposition regarding power, water, and job impacts, with only 60-65% of pipeline projects expected to proceed as scheduled.",
   "Skilled labor shortages, particularly for high-voltage electricians and substation crews, are acting as a major bottleneck, forcing a shift toward modular 'data center in a box' solutions.",
   "Power generation lead times remain extended (up to 2030 for turbines), though pricing growth is moderating due to new capacity and equipment availability from canceled projects.",
   "OEMs are tightening contract terms, including higher down payments (20% vs 10%) and first right of refusal clauses to protect backlog quality.",
